<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  FORGE_SLOT_DECIDE_NEEDS_A_DESCRIPTION. The dhoggur fills the Forge's small ground-animal slot that the crescendo
  anole (AA_CrescendoAnole) leaves; owner by card 2026-10-16, his description verbatim: "a bizarre creature that
  constantly snuffles and digs at the ashy minerals freshly deposited by volcanic sputter. Very tough heat resistant
  hide." Invented name, free RM_ tier, ONE HOME: the Forge (row in RM_TheForge_Biome.xml at the anole's 0.5).
  Art installed through the art ledger at the texPath below (east/south/north, artpipe forgeslot_dhoggur_v1).

  DHOGGUR_USE_DECIDE_SNUFFLING_FOR_A_JOB (owner 2026-10-16): "improve the Dhoggur to take advantage of some of the old
  Crescendo anole concept: if you mess with it, it swells with violent chemical reactions that make it three times as
  big and spewing fire (firespit). Stays that way for 1/3 of a day, then it can't do it again for another day. Super
  aggressive when angered, but otherwise totally docile and placid while foraging."
  - CompProperties_DhoggurSwell + RM_DhoggurSwell hediff + the RM_DhoggurSwellBody render tree (Source/RM_ForgeDhoggurSwell.cs).
  - Docile otherwise: manhunterOnDamageChance / manhunterOnTameFailChance 0 (the swell is its only anger), a wild
    herbivore that grazes and flees as vanilla does when the swell is spent or switched off.
  Numbers PROVISIONAL.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Dhoggur</defName>
    <label>dhoggur</label>
    <description>A bizarre creature that constantly snuffles and digs at the ashy minerals freshly deposited by volcanic sputter. Its hide is very tough and heat resistant.</description>
